<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI says Memphis top world cargo airport in Jan-Ap.</title>
<headline>ACI says Memphis top world cargo airport in Jan-Ap.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in January-April 1997, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI) in a survey of 496 airports worldwide.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in January-April 1997, with the volume they handled, their ranking and the percentage change on January-April 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>     1 (1)  Memphis	     692,024    up 20.7 pct</p>
<p>     2 (3)  Los Angeles	 586,313    up 10.1</p>
<p>     3 (2)  Miami		 561,233    up  3.4</p>
<p>     4 (4)  Tokyo-Narita	549,622    up  7.7</p>
<p>     5 (7)  Hong Kong	   540,445    up 17.9</p>
<p>     6 (5)  New York -JFK     519,067    up  1.9</p>
<p>     7 (8)  Seoul		 492,290    up 19.5</p>
<p>     8 (6)  Frankfurt	   488,545    up  2.0</p>
<p>     9 (7)  Louisville	  444,984  down  1.0</p>
<p>    10 (10) Singapore	   429,622    up 15.1</p>
<p>    11 (9)  Chicago	     419,269    up 10.9</p>
<p>    12 (11) Amsterdam	   390,326    up  4.8</p>
<p>    13 (13) Anchorage*	  384,275    up 20.3</p>
<p>    14 (12) London Heathrow   380,319    up  5.0</p>
<p>    15 (14) Paris CDG	   328,209    up  5.3</p>
<p>    16 (15) New York-Newark   324,183    up  6.8</p>
<p>    17 (19) Taipei		274,874    up 18.0</p>
<p>    18 (16) Atlanta	     266,422    up  4.5</p>
<p>    19 (17) Dallas Fort Worth 263,974    up  9.0</p>
<p>    20 (18) Dayton		256,738    up  8.3</p>
<p>* includes freight and mail in transit as well as loaded +</p>
<p>	 loaded</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
